1 NOTE Great-grandfather of Miles and his namesake. Full name Miles Brewton Hutson -
2 CONT "Miles Brewton" is a celebrated Charleston name (the Miles Brewton House,
2 CONT 1769), reflecting the family's South Carolina low-country roots. Born in
2 CONT South Carolina, son of Confederate veteran, professor and artist Charles
2 CONT Woodward Hutson; raised partly in Texas while his father taught there. Married
2 CONT Louise Adela Nelson on 19 July 1919. In 1950 an electrical engineer living at
2 CONT 321 Hillary Street, New Orleans, with Adela and son Richard Neil. His sister
2 CONT Mary Lockett Hutson married Bernard Stanley Nelson (1913) - a second
2 CONT Hutson-Nelson marriage in the same generation.
2 CONT UNCONFIRMED MENTIONS (same name, plausible but not proven to be him): "Miles
2 CONT B. Hutson, a Junior" at Texas A&M in 1908 (The History of the A.&M. College
2 CONT Trouble, 1908) and "2d Lieut. M. B. Hutson" in 1918 War Department orders.
2 SOUR @S28@
3 _CONF Secondary
2 SOUR @S13@
3 _CONF Primary
