1 TITL Hutson surname - etymology and history
1 PUBL WikiTree surname study; House of Names; archives.com
1 _URL https://www.wikitree.com/genealogy/HUTSON
1 _CONF Secondary
1 _ACC 2026-07-11
1 NOTE English patronymic surname derived from the medieval given name "Hudde"
2 CONT (a pet form of Hugh, "heart/mind," or a variant of Hudson). First recorded
2 CONT as William Hudde in the 1273 Hundred Rolls of Cambridgeshire, England.
2 CONT General surname background only - NOT evidence of this family's specific line.
0 @S4@ SOUR
1 TITL Obituary of Richard Neil Hutson (1928-2017)
1 AUTH North Dallas Funeral Home & Cremations, Dallas, Texas
1 PUBL northdallasfuneralhome.com, September 2017
1 _URL https://www.northdallasfuneralhome.com/obituaries/Hutson-Richard-Neil?obId=31321155
1 _CONF Secondary
1 _ACC 2026-07-11
1 NOTE The anchor document for the paternal line. Establishes: death 20 Sep 2017 at
2 CONT age 89; birth in New Orleans to Miles and Adela Hutson; three older sisters
2 CONT Louise Finke, Charlene Wilke, Mary Jane Trapolin; Jesuit HS and Tulane (M.S.
2 CONT E.E. at age 20); WWII shipboard radar service; Chief Engineer at Chance
2 CONT Vought Electronics; founder of Hutson Corporation (1964); inventor of the
2 CONT world's smallest pistol scope; wife of 56 years Joan Liebes Hutson; children
2 CONT John Charles (Hilary), Paul Neil (Nicole), Mary Louise Suttles (Sonny);
2 CONT grandchildren Zachary, Miles, Sydnie, Jennifer, Casey, Shelley, Carter, Cole.
