1 NOTE Great-great-grandfather of Miles. Son of Herman Liebes, founder of H. Liebes
2 CONT & Co. Treasurer (1905) and later vice-president of the family firm; a member
2 CONT of the Concordia and Argonaut clubs and a civic leader. On Sunday 2 July
2 CONT 1916, on vacation at Long Beach, he carried his 13-year-old son George into
2 CONT the surf; a rip tide pulled both under. A lifeguard rescued George, but
2 CONT Julien was found clinging to a pier piling and died despite first aid, as his
2 CONT wife and younger son Martin watched. His widow Sophie was appointed
2 CONT administratrix of his estate (about $40,000).
