1 NOTE Great-great-grandfather of Miles. Grew up on plantations near McPhersonville
2 CONT in Beaufort District, S.C.; attended South Carolina College; served in the
2 CONT Confederate army throughout the Civil War (his wartime letters home are
2 CONT widely cited by historians). Married Mary Jane Lockett on 5 July 1871.
2 CONT Taught in several Southern states including fifteen years in Texas, then
2 CONT settled in New Orleans, where he became known late in life as a painter and
2 CONT writer; he edited several posthumous collections of Lafcadio Hearn's New
2 CONT Orleans writings (Creole Sketches, Fantastics, Editorials). His papers
2 CONT (1765-1949) are held by the Southern Historical Collection, UNC Chapel Hill
2 CONT (#00362), and his notes on the Lockett family underpin the 1951 genealogy.
