1 NOTE 7x-great-grandmother of Miles (pronounced "Ro-shay"). Family tradition -
2 CONT the "Little Nightcap" story - holds that as a young Huguenot she was
2 CONT smuggled out of Catholic France hidden in a cask and carried to Amsterdam,
2 CONT where her sisters received her; her younger sister Jeanne had married in
2 CONT London in 1689. She married Abraham Michaux at Amsterdam in 1692 and died in
2 CONT Virginia before December 1744. The 1951 Lockett genealogy misspells her
2 CONT surname "Richet."
