1 NOTE First-person account by Miles Brewton Hutson's sister: "As a child in
2 CONT Texas I had a bed of old blue flags ... When we moved to New Orleans in 1908,
2 CONT my sister, Ethel Hutson, who was already here studying art under Dr.
2 CONT Ellsworth Woodward at Newcomb College, told us about the wonderful field of
2 CONT irises out on Frenchman Street ... my sister-in-law, Adela Nelson, told me
2 CONT that as a child she used to go there on her uncle's back looking for
2 CONT irises." She was secretary of the New Orleans Garden Society about 1920.
