2 SOUR @S43@
3 _CONF Secondary
1 NOTE 9x-great-grandfather of Miles and the origin of the family name "Miles
2 CONT Brewton." Arrived in Carolina as a boy in 1684; became a goldsmith, which then
2 CONT meant banker; distinguished himself in the 1709 governorship riot; was
2 CONT foreman of the grand jury that tried the pirate STEDE BONNET and his crew in
2 CONT October 1718; served on the committee investigating the 1740 St. Augustine
2 CONT expedition. Married three times; his first wife (Robert's mother) is unknown.
2 CONT Parents unknown (possibly a Robert Bruton of Andover who sailed for Barbados
2 CONT in 1640 - speculative).
2 SOUR @S43@
3 _CONF Secondary
