1 TITL "The Huguenot Abraham Michaux and Descendants"
1 AUTH Eggleston, J. D.
1 PUBL Virginia Magazine of History and Biography, vol. 44, no. 4 (Oct. 1936), pp. 363ff., continued vol. 45, no. 1 (Jan. 1937); Internet Archive
1 _URL https://archive.org/details/sim_virginia-magazine-of-history-and-biography_1936-10_44_4
1 _CONF Secondary
1 _ACC 2026-09-23
1 NOTE Scholarly genealogy correcting earlier Michaux traditions. Its French
2 CONT pedigrees come from the Huguenot church registers of Sedan, searched by
2 CONT Pasteur U. Weiss of the Societe de l'Histoire du Protestantisme Francais, and
2 CONT from Amsterdam Walloon-church records supplied by elder H. F. Baerselman.
2 CONT Gives the Michaux (Abraham 1608 -> Jacob 1644 -> Abraham 1672-1717),
2 CONT Severin (Nicholas -> Paul 1615 -> Anne 1649), de Serignon and Rochet (Thomas
2 CONT -> Thiery 1615 -> Jean -> Suzanne bap. 1667) lines, and identifies Ann
2 CONT Madelin Michaux (b. c. 1710/11) as wife of Richard Woodson of "Poplar Hill"
2 CONT and mother of Agnes Woodson, wife of Francis Watkins, clerk of Prince Edward
2 CONT County. Continuation: archive.org/details/sim_virginia-magazine-of-history-
2 CONT and-biography_1937-01_45_1.
