3 _CONF Secondary
1 NOTE 7x-great-grandfather of Miles. Planter of Henrico (later Chesterfield)
2 CONT County on Swift Creek and Nuttree Run; his will (signed 1749, probated 1760)
2 CONT leaves "to my granddaughter, Mary Clay, daughter of Charles Clay (afterwards
2 CONT Mrs. Stephen Lockett), one negro girl, named Phoebe" - the enslaved people
2 CONT named in these wills are part of this family's history. The 1899 Clay
2 CONT history calls him "the common ancestor of the Clays of Kentucky," grandfather
2 CONT of Gen. Green Clay and of the statesman Henry Clay of Ashland; the latter
2 CONT claim is the book's, not independently verified here.
2 SOUR @S45@
3 _CONF Secondary
